Package: xlkit
Title: Read and Write Excel Workbooks, Naming Cells as Excel Shows Them
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Bearak", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jbearak@guttmacher.org")
Description: Reads .xlsx workbooks into tibbles, naming sheets, ranges
    and header rows as Excel shows them. Each column's type comes from
    every cell in it; cells that do not fit and Excel errors are reported
    with their cell references. Dates follow each cell's number format
    and the workbook's date system. Writes data frames to new workbooks,
    one sheet each or several tables on one sheet, with a bold header
    that stays in view, fitted column widths, number formats, styles and
    Stata's variable and value labels, and never replaces a file unless
    told to. Reading is done in Rust by the calamine crate and writing by
    the rust_xlsxwriter crate.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/jbearak/xlkit
